class.description:
The expression node computes a value from its inputs. [member expression] is a Godot [Expression]; every name in [member input_names] becomes a data input port of that name (type: any), and can be used as a variable in the expression. The single data output port is [code]result[/code], with the type [member result_type]. The node has no flow ports, so it is evaluated on demand when another node reads its [code]result[/code].
The ports follow [member input_names] and [member result_type] automatically. If you change them while connections exist, connections to ports that no longer exist are reported by [method FlowGraph.validate] as [constant FlowGraphValidation.ISSUE_KIND_UNKNOWN_PORT]. An empty or unparsable expression is reported as a configuration warning ([method FlowNode.get_configuration_warnings]).
At runtime the expression is evaluated on demand, each time a node reads [code]result[/code] through [FlowGraphPlayback]. An input that is connected reads the connected data output. An unconnected input reads the blackboard variable of the same name if it exists, otherwise [code]null[/code], so [code]gold >= 10[/code] works without a [FlowGetVariableNode]. The [Expression] is parsed once and cached; it is parsed again after [member expression] or [member input_names] change. It runs without a base instance, so it sees its inputs and global functions only. A parse error prints an error; a failed execution gives [code]null[/code].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var expression := FlowExpressionNode.new()
expression.input_names = PackedStringArray(["gold", "price"])
expression.expression = "gold >= price"
expression.result_type = TYPE_BOOL
var expression_id := graph.add_node(expression)
graph.connect_nodes(expression_id, "result", branch_id, "condition")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var expression = new FlowExpressionNode
{
    InputNames = ["gold", "price"],
    Expression = "gold >= price",
    ResultType = Variant.Type.Bool,
};
int expressionId = graph.AddNode(expression);
graph.ConnectNodes(expressionId, "result", branchId, "condition");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
